   "line": [
    "b3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The dark bishop is awkward everywhere — Bf4 runs into Nxd4 and e5, Bg5 is kicked by h6, Bd2 hangs the knight. When you're unsure where a piece belongs, one answer is not to develop it there at all. We fianchettoed one bishop — why not the other? b3.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "When no good square exists for a bishop, consider a second fianchetto rather than forcing a bad developing move."
