   "line": [
    "Ndb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Ndb5 is the precise execution — sacrifice just one knight, not both, and exploit Black's queen. After axb5, Nxb5 hits the queen, and then Bxg7 tears the king open. The move order is everything; the other knight to b5 would let Black decline.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "In a knight sacrifice, choose the piece and order that also attacks the queen, denying the defender a decline."
